---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the Instant Chefs website handles your staffing enquiry: contact form delivery through FormSubmit, WhatsApp, email, Instagram and map links."
  cta={false}
>
  <PageHero
    label="Privacy policy"
    title="Your enquiry. Handled with care."
    text="This page explains how information is handled by this website and the contact channels you choose to use."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <article class="container legal-content">
      <h2>Information you choose to share</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form asks for your name, email address, phone number and a
        message, and for your agreement to this policy. You may also provide
        your location, business or household type, staff and cuisine
        requirement, preferred plan, experience requirement and salary range.
        Please share only information relevant to your staffing enquiry.
      </p>
      <h2>How the contact form is processed</h2>
      <p>
        When you press “Send enquiry”, the details you entered are sent to
        <a
          href="https://formsubmit.co/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          FormSubmit
        </a>
        , a third-party form service, which delivers them by email to the
        Instant Chefs Gmail inbox ({business.email}). FormSubmit and Google
        (Gmail) process that information under their own privacy terms. This
        website does not store your enquiry in its own database or in browser
        storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        FormSubmit may show a short spam check before delivering your message.
        If you choose “Send via WhatsApp” instead, the details you entered are
        passed to WhatsApp as a draft message for you to review and send;
        WhatsApp handles that information under its own privacy terms.
      </p>
      <h2>When you contact the team</h2>
      <p>
        Information you send through the contact form, WhatsApp, email or a
        phone conversation is used by the team to understand your staffing
        requirement and respond to your enquiry. Before candidate interviews,
        discuss with the team which details need to be shared for hiring
        coordination.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies, browser storage and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This implementation does not set advertising or analytics cookies, and
        does not use browser storage to retain your form details. Fonts and
        website photographs are served with the website. The hosting provider
        may process technical request information such as IP addresses and
        browser information to deliver and protect the website.
      </p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to WhatsApp, Instagram and Google Maps take you to third-party
        services. Email links open your chosen email application. Each service
        controls its own data handling. A map is not embedded on this website;
        you choose when to open directions.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions about your information</h2>
      <p>
        Contact Instant Chefs at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or{' '}
        <a href={business.tel}>{business.phone}</a> to ask about information you
        have shared, request a correction or discuss deletion. Please avoid
        including sensitive personal documents in an initial enquiry.
      </p>
      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        If analytics or other integrations are added, this policy will be
        updated to reflect how those services handle information.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
